Argument in Favor of Measure J
REBUILD ORANGE: STRONGER FINANCES. SAFER NEIGHBORHOODS.
A BETTER FUTURE.
Measure J is a simple idea: hotel guests should pay their fair share of taxes
for City of Orange services because Orange residents should not bear the
entire cost of serving hotel guests.
Every day, visitors staying in Orange hotels rely on our police officers,
firefighters, streets, parks, and other public services. Measure J simply
asks visitors to contribute more toward the community they enjoy.
Our major neighbors – Anaheim, Garden Grove, Santa Ana, and Tustin –
all charge higher hotel taxes than we do. Even increasing to 14%, Orange
will remain competitive with neighboring cities that already charge equal
or higher hotel tax rates.
Orange’s hotel tax was last updated in 1993. Measure J modernizes
outdated tax rules and updates the tax for larger hotels. Measure J ensures
all hotel guests are treated equally: travelers shouldn’t be exempt
from hotel tax just for booking their rooms through online travel
companies, like Expedia and Priceline, simply because that technology
didn’t exist in 1993.
